# Runtime dependencies (installed on Render) — the SOURCE of `requirements.txt`.
#
# Edit this file, never the .txt: `requirements.txt` is the frozen lockfile
# Render installs (§10 Phase 14's dependency freeze), compiled from here. After
# an edit, recompile every lock in one go, from backend/:
#
#     uv pip compile requirements-dev.in --universal --python-version 3.11 -o requirements-dev.txt
#     uv pip compile requirements.in -c requirements-dev.txt --universal --python-version 3.11 -o requirements.txt
#     uv pip compile requirements-research.in -c requirements-dev.txt --universal --python-version 3.11 -o requirements-research.txt
#     uv pip compile requirements-notebooks.in -c requirements-dev.txt --universal --python-version 3.11 -o requirements-notebooks.txt
#
# The dev lock is resolved first and the others are constrained by it, so all
# four pin one version of every package. `--universal` with 3.11 as the floor
# gives one file valid on the research machine's 3.11, CI's 3.12 and Render's
# 3.14 (REPLICATION.md §2). `test_requirement_locks` checks that every pin
# satisfies the range declared here.
#
# Declared as compatible ranges; the exact pins are in the lock. The free-tier
# RAM budget is 512 MB (§8).

